# Linear ⇆ Cursor sync

This project is tracked in Linear team **Domagoj** (key `DOM`, workspace `domagojp`) via the Linear MCP tools. Keep Linear and the codebase in sync on every run **without the user having to ask**. Skip only for trivial, non-project chats (quick questions, explanations) or when the user says "skip linear".

Linear MCP is allowlisted in `.cursor/permissions.json` so Auto-run should not prompt for every Linear read/write. Do not ask the user to approve individual Linear tool calls.

Also follow project skill `.cursor/skills/linear-workflow/SKILL.md` when creating or sizing issues.

## A. Pull from Linear first (ask before acting)

At the **start** of any substantive coding/planning task:

1. Read the ISO timestamp in `.cursor/linear-sync-state.json` (`lastSyncedAt`). If the file is missing, treat now as the baseline and create it.
2. Call `list_issues` (team `Domagoj`, `updatedAt` = that timestamp, `orderBy: updatedAt`) to find issues **created or changed since the last sync** — i.e. anything the user added/edited directly in Linear, not through Cursor.
3. If any are found, **stop and ask** before proceeding — list them compactly (ID, title, status) and ask: *"These changed in Linear since we last synced — should I factor them into this task?"* Use the question tool. Do not silently absorb them.
4. Only incorporate the ones the user confirms. After the user answers, write the current ISO time back to `lastSyncedAt`.
5. If nothing changed, continue silently.

## B. Push to Linear as work happens (automatic)

Keep Linear reflecting reality — no need to be asked:

- **Starting an issue:** move it to `In Progress` (or create the branch from the issue's git branch name).
- **Finishing meaningful work:** short comment optional; move toward `Done`. Prefer `Fixes DOM-<n>` in the PR.
- **New scope / no ticket:** create the issue (`save_issue`, team `Domagoj`, assignee `me`, project + one `Area` + type label), then proceed. Mention the new ID.
- **Plans change:** update issue/project description — don't leave Linear stale.

### Issue size (required)

- One issue = one closable outcome. If you can't mark Done without reading a comment thread, split it.
- Too big for one issue, too small for a project → **parent + sub-issues** (Linear `parentId`).
- Projects = milestones (M0–M4). Don't invent projects for single spikes.
- **Comments are not a task list.** Use for decisions, blockers, or a 1–3 line status. Put durable findings in repo docs / Linear Documents. Prefer ticking checklists / closing sub-issues over long diaries.

### Checklists

Markdown checklists (`- [ ]` / `- [x]`) do not update themselves. After progress: `get_issue` → `save_issue` with boxes updated. Tick only when that item's acceptance is met. If code landed but validation is pending, leave unchecked and use a short `## Progress` note. Never mark Done until all boxes + `## Done when` are satisfied (for parents: all sub-issues Done).

## C. Conventions

- One `Area` label per issue: `infra`, `extraction`, `ui`, `suggestions`, `nano`, `smart-mode`, `privacy-security`, `a11y-polish`, `docs-release`.
- Projects: `M0 · Technical Validation` … `M4 · Safety, Polish & Release`.
- Never invent Linear IDs — confirm via tools.
